{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/jing/content/step.cljc | sed -n '1,590p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.jing.content.step\n     2\t  \"The stepped client half of the content service (docs/design/\n     3\t   dao.stream.remote.md section 5, the Linda request medium;\n     4\t   dao.jing.content holds the vocabulary). The portable interface, per\n     5\t   dao.stream.md OD-5: a pure client the caller steps, with the\n     6\t   request-put / request-get / request-materialize / step / abandon\n     7\t   shape the deleted dao.jing.remote.step carried, over a requests\n     8\t   writer and an answers reader that are reflections or local handles.\n     9\t\n    10\t   Everything here is a pure function over explicit data. No socket,\n    11\t   atom, promise, callback, or scheduler. The caller owns the state,\n    12\t   attaches it to whatever pair it has, and chooses every cadence.\n    13\t\n    14\t   The state is {:requests w :answers r :cursor c :unsent u\n    15\t   :outstanding {s request} :completed [...] :diagnostics [...]\n    16\t   :terminal nil :materializations {put-id record} :routes {live-id\n    17\t   put-id}}. A cursor is either one the answers reader handed out or an\n    18\t   anchor keyword -- :dao.stream/newest, the Linda mint -- which the\n    19\t   first poll resolves through the reader, retrying while the reader\n    20\t   answers a retryable mint (a reflection's cursor ask). A materialization\n    21\t   record is {:phase :put|:verify-unissued|:verify-issued :address a\n    22\t   :put-id s :get-id m?} -- an address, never a payload: nothing this\n    23\t   layer retains or publishes carries a payload. :routes maps every\n    24\t   answer id a record currently claims to the record's put id, which is\n    25\t   the identity a materialization's one published completion carries.\n    26\t\n    27\t   step advances in one fixed order, and the order is load-bearing:\n    28\t\n    29\t   1. re-append the retained :unsent request (a writer that answered\n    30\t      full), folding the outcome under :attempt;\n    31\t   2. poll at most `budget` answers, correlating each by :jing/request,\n    32\t      filing unknown or malformed values as diagnostics;\n    33\t   3. on a terminal reader, lose the retained request with the terminal\n    34\t      reason, so its loss surfaces on the ordinary completion path;\n    35\t   4. issue the unissued verify reads of :verify-unissued records, in\n    36\t      the order their puts were issued, until the writer answers full\n    37\t      or the reader ends;\n    38\t   5. route every completion: a found get answer and a :present verify\n    39\t      pass through the one ingress check dao.jing/accept-bytes! before\n    40\t      any value is published.\n    41\t\n    42\t   The verify hop is the one obligation the client carries for\n    43\t   materialization: a put answering :present has promised that equal\n    44\t   content sits at the address, and a remote server is not trusted to\n    45\t   have kept that promise. So :present publishes nothing; the record\n    46\t   moves to :verify-unissued, a correlated read is issued by order 4,\n    47\t   and only a read-back that verifies against the address completes\n    48\t   :result :present. The record's removal is the exactly-once guard:\n    49\t   one completion per materialization, carrying the put id.\n    50\t\n    51\t   Reattachment stays the caller's: after a terminal reason every\n    52\t   further request answers :terminal, and a new pair is a new client.\n    53\t   abandon retires only the retained :unsent request -- the one delivery\n    54\t   this binding still owes.\"\n    55\t  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n    56\t            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n    57\t            [dao.stream :as stream]))\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\t;; =============================================================================\n    61\t;; Vocabulary\n    62\t;; =============================================================================\n    63\t\n    64\t\n    65\t(def get-op\n    66\t  \"The read operation this client speaks.\"\n    67\t  :jing/get)\n    68\t\n    69\t\n    70\t(def put-op\n    71\t  \"The write operation this client speaks.\"\n    72\t  :jing/put)\n    73\t\n    74\t\n    75\t(def malformed-response-code\n    76\t  \"The error code for an answer that does not conform to its request's\n    77\t   wire vocabulary -- a get not answering the exact found?/bytes shape,\n    78\t   a put not answering :inserted or :present.\"\n    79\t  :dao.jing.content/malformed-response)\n    80\t\n    81\t\n    82\t(def integrity-failure-code\n    83\t  \"The error code for content that fails the ingress check on arrival:\n    84\t   a found read-back that does not hash to the address it was read from,\n    85\t   or bytes that are not one canonical payload.\"\n    86\t  :dao.jing.content/integrity-failure)\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\t(def present-but-absent-code\n    90\t  \"The error code for a put that answered :present and a verify read\n    91\t   that then found nothing at the address.\"\n    92\t  :dao.jing.content/present-but-absent)\n    93\t\n    94\t\n    95\t(def abandoned-code\n    96\t  \"The default abandon reason: this layer's own word for a request given\n    97\t   up by policy rather than lost by the medium.\"\n    98\t  :dao.jing.content/abandoned)\n    99\t\n   100\t\n   101\t(def ^:private integrity-failure\n   102\t  \"The error map a failed ingress check publishes, by code.\"\n   103\t  {:code integrity-failure-code\n   104\t   :message \"the remote content does not hash to its content address\"})\n   105\t\n   106\t\n   107\t(def ^:private malformed-response\n   108\t  \"The error map for an answer outside its request's vocabulary.\"\n   109\t  {:code malformed-response-code\n   110\t   :message \"the answer does not conform to the request's vocabulary\"})\n   111\t\n   112\t\n   113\t(def ^:private present-but-absent\n   114\t  {:code present-but-absent-code\n   115\t   :message \"the remote reported :present but the content address is absent\"})\n   116\t\n   117\t\n   118\t(defn- mint-id\n   119\t  \"A self-minted random request id, unique against this client's live\n   120\t   ids so callers sharing one answers stream do not collide.\"\n   121\t  [state]\n   122\t  (loop []\n   123\t    (let [id (str (random-uuid))]\n   124\t      (if (or (contains? (:outstanding state) id)\n   125\t              (= id (get-in state [:unsent :id])))\n   126\t        (recur)\n   127\t        id))))\n   128\t\n   129\t\n   130\t(defn- answer?\n   131\t  \"True for any well-formed answer value: the request id key, whatever\n   132\t   body follows it.\"\n   133\t  [v]\n   134\t  (and (map? v) (contains? v :jing/request)))\n   135\t\n   136\t\n   137\t;; =============================================================================\n   138\t;; State\n   139\t;; =============================================================================\n   140\t\n   141\t\n   142\t(defn client-state\n   143\t  \"The stepped client's state over one content pair: `requests` the\n   144\t   writer the client appends its requests to, `answers` the reader it\n   145\t   polls, `cursor` either a cursor `answers` handed out or an anchor\n   146\t   keyword (:dao.stream/newest, the Linda mint, resolved on the first\n   147\t   poll -- a reflection's mint is answered across the channel, so the\n   148\t   first steps may retry it). The caller owns the result and every step\n   149\t   of it.\"\n   150\t  [requests answers cursor]\n   151\t  {:requests requests\n   152\t   :answers answers\n   153\t   :cursor cursor\n   154\t   :unsent nil\n   155\t   :outstanding {}\n   156\t   :completed []\n   157\t   :diagnostics []\n   158\t   :terminal nil\n   159\t   :next-seq 0\n   160\t   :materializations {}\n   161\t   :routes {}})\n   162\t\n   163\t\n   164\t(defn- segment-address!\n   165\t  \"Throw unless `address` is a segment address: arbitrary keys and\n   166\t   mutable roots are refused before the wire.\"\n   167\t  [address]\n   168\t  (when-not (jing/segment-address? address)\n   169\t    (throw (ex-info \"a stepped content request names a non-segment address\"\n   170\t                    {:address address}))))\n   171\t\n   172\t\n   173\t(defn- register\n   174\t  \"Claim `id` for a materialization: the record (carrying its issue\n   175\t   order under :seq -- the ids are random, so the order the verify reads\n   176\t   issue in is the record's own) and its route.\"\n   177\t  [state id address]\n   178\t  (-> state\n   179\t      (assoc-in [:materializations id]\n   180\t                {:phase :put, :address address, :put-id id\n   181\t                 :seq (:next-seq state)})\n   182\t      (update :next-seq (fnil inc 0))\n   183\t      (assoc-in [:routes id] id)))\n   184\t\n   185\t\n   186\t(defn- submit\n   187\t  \"The shared body of the request entry points: answer :terminal on a\n   188\t   client whose answers reader has ended (a new pair is a new client),\n   189\t   refuse with :busy while an unsent request is owed (only step's order\n   190\t   1 clears it), append the request value, and register a\n   191\t   materialization record at any id the writer's answer carries. A\n   192\t   writer refusal completes at once -- the record routes that loss at\n   193\t   the next drain.\"\n   194\t  [state request materialize?]\n   195\t  (cond\n   196\t    (:terminal state)\n   197\t    {:outcome :terminal, :state state}\n   198\t\n   199\t    (:unsent state)\n   200\t    {:outcome :busy, :state state}\n   201\t\n   202\t    :else\n   203\t    (let [id (mint-id state)\n   204\t          value (assoc request :jing/request id)\n   205\t          result (stream/append! (:requests state) value)\n   206\t          outcome (:dao.stream/outcome result)\n   207\t          address (get request put-op)]\n   208\t      (cond\n   209\t        (= :dao.stream/ok outcome)\n   210\t        {:outcome :requested\n   211\t         :state (-> (assoc-in state [:outstanding id] request)\n   212\t                    (cond-> materialize? (register id address)))\n   213\t         :id id}\n   214\t\n   215\t        (= :dao.stream/full outcome)\n   216\t        {:outcome :pending-request\n   217\t         :state (-> (assoc state :unsent {:id id, :value value})\n   218\t                    (cond-> materialize? (register id address)))\n   219\t         :id id}\n   220\t\n   221\t        :else\n   222\t        ;; closed, invalid-value, transport-error: the append never\n   223\t        ;; happened; the loss completes on the ordinary path\n   224\t        {:outcome :request-undeliverable\n   225\t         :state (-> (update state :completed\n   226\t                            conj {:id id, :request request, :lost outcome})\n   227\t                    (cond-> materialize? (register id address)))\n   228\t         :id id\n   229\t         :reason outcome}))))\n   230\t\n   231\t\n   232\t;; =============================================================================\n   233\t;; The request entry points\n   234\t;; =============================================================================\n   235\t\n   236\t\n   237\t(defn request-get\n   238\t  \"Request one remote read of `address`. A non-segment address throws\n   239\t   before the wire. While an unsent request is owed the answer is\n   240\t   {:outcome :busy :state s} and nothing was submitted; otherwise the\n   241\t   outcome is returned with the minted id under :id, and the read's\n   242\t   completion arrives through step as {:id s :found? b :value v} (or an\n   243\t   :error, or a :lost tail).\"\n   244\t  [state address]\n   245\t  (segment-address! address)\n   246\t  (submit state {get-op address} false))\n   247\t\n   248\t\n   249\t(defn request-put\n   250\t  \"Request one remote put of `payload` at `address`. A non-segment\n   251\t   address throws before the wire; address-against-payload validation is\n   252\t   the server's at its own door, and a mismatch is the server's silence.\n   253\t   A plain put publishes :result :inserted or :result :present with no\n   254\t   verify read: the read-back is materialization's obligation.\"\n   255\t  [state address payload]\n   256\t  (segment-address! address)\n   257\t  (submit state {put-op address\n   258\t                 :jing/bytes (jing/bytes->base64\n   259\t                               (jing/canonical-bytes payload))}\n   260\t          false))\n   261\t\n   262\t\n   263\t(defn request-put-bytes\n   264\t  \"The bytes-level twin of request-put for a caller already holding the\n   265\t   canonical payload bytes -- the byte-store handle's own put. The bytes\n   266\t   must hash to `address`; the server's ingress check refuses them\n   267\t   otherwise, and a refused request is the server's silence.\"\n   268\t  [state address bs]\n   269\t  (segment-address! address)\n   270\t  (submit state {put-op address\n   271\t                 :jing/bytes (jing/bytes->base64 bs)}\n   272\t          false))\n   273\t\n   274\t\n   275\t(defn request-materialize\n   276\t  \"Request one remote materialization of `payload`: the address is\n   277\t   derived here, the put is submitted, and the returned :id is the put\n   278\t   id the one completion will carry. Supports an explicit algorithm via\n   279\t   opts: {:algorithm :sha256}.\"\n   280\t  ([state payload] (request-materialize state payload {}))\n   281\t  ([state payload opts]\n   282\t   (let [bs (jing/canonical-bytes payload)\n   283\t         algo (get opts :algorithm jing/default-hash-algorithm)\n   284\t         reg (get jing/registry algo)]\n   285\t     (when-not reg\n   286\t       (throw (ex-info (str \"unsupported hash algorithm: \" algo)\n   287\t                       {:algorithm algo})))\n   288\t     (let [address (keyword \"segment\"\n   289\t                            (str (:address-id reg)\n   290\t                                 \"-\" (jing/digest-bytes algo bs)))]\n   291\t       (submit state {put-op address\n   292\t                      :jing/bytes (jing/bytes->base64 bs)}\n   293\t               true)))))\n   294\t\n   295\t\n   296\t(def ^:private refused\n   297\t  \"The ingress-refusal sentinel for the strict receipt decode below: one\n   298\t   opaque host object held by this single var, so every reference to it\n   299\t   is the same instance on every host. A keyword literal cannot serve:\n   300\t   on cljs each literal site compiles to a fresh Keyword object, so an\n   301\t   `identical?` across two sites misses, and a refused decode escaped\n   302\t   into the value arm. The closed CBOR profile never decodes a host\n   303\t   object, so no decoded value can be this; the sentinel itself is what\n   304\t   distinguishes a refused reply from a stored nil, which decodes to the\n   305\t   value nil.\"\n   306\t  #?(:cljd (Object.)\n   307\t     :clj (Object.)\n   308\t     :cljs (js-obj)))\n   309\t\n   310\t\n   311\t(defn- accepted-value\n   312\t  \"The value a found get answer carries, admitted through the one\n   313\t   ingress check (dao.jing/accept-bytes!) and decoded, or `refused` when\n   314\t   the check refuses it.\"\n   315\t  [address b64]\n   316\t  (try\n   317\t    (cbor/decode (jing/accept-bytes! address b64))\n   318\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   319\t      refused)))\n   320\t\n   321\t\n   322\t;; =============================================================================\n   323\t;; Completion decode\n   324\t;; =============================================================================\n   325\t\n   326\t\n   327\t(defn- get-answer?\n   328\t  \"True only for the exact read answer {:jing/request r :jing/found? b\n   329\t   :jing/bytes b64}.\"\n   330\t  [v]\n   331\t  (and (map? v)\n   332\t       (= #{:jing/request :jing/found? :jing/bytes} (set (keys v)))\n   333\t       (let [f (get v :jing/found?)] (or (true? f) (false? f)))))\n   334\t\n   335\t\n   336\t(defn- put-answer?\n   337\t  \"True only for the exact write answer {:jing/request r\n   338\t   :jing/result v}.\"\n   339\t  [v]\n   340\t  (and (map? v) (= #{:jing/request :jing/result} (set (keys v)))))\n   341\t\n   342\t\n   343\t(defn- decode-plain-completion\n   344\t  \"Total decode of one completion no materialization claims: the answer\n   345\t   conforms to its request's vocabulary or the completion carries an\n   346\t   :error; a loss carries :lost.\"\n   347\t  [completion]\n   348\t  (let [{:keys [id request lost answer]} completion]\n   349\t    (cond\n   350\t      lost {:id id, :lost lost}\n   351\t\n   352\t      (contains? request get-op)\n   353\t      (cond\n   354\t        (not (get-answer? answer)) {:id id, :error malformed-response}\n   355\t        (not (get answer :jing/found?))\n   356\t        {:id id, :found? false, :value nil}\n   357\t        :else\n   358\t        (let [value (accepted-value (get request get-op)\n   359\t                                    (get answer :jing/bytes))]\n   360\t          (if (identical? refused value)\n   361\t            {:id id, :error integrity-failure}\n   362\t            {:id id, :found? true, :value value})))\n   363\t\n   364\t      :else\n   365\t      (if (and (put-answer? answer)\n   366\t               (#{:inserted :present} (get answer :jing/result)))\n   367\t        {:id id, :address (get request put-op),\n   368\t         :result (get answer :jing/result)}\n   369\t        {:id id, :error malformed-response}))))\n   370\t\n   371\t\n   372\t;; =============================================================================\n   373\t;; The materialization transition\n   374\t;; =============================================================================\n   375\t\n   376\t\n   377\t(defn- materialization-entry\n   378\t  \"The published tail of one materialization completion: the put id, the\n   379\t   marker, and the address -- never the payload.\"\n   380\t  [record]\n   381\t  {:id (get record :put-id)\n   382\t   :materialized? true\n   383\t   :address (get record :address)})\n   384\t\n   385\t\n   386\t(defn- materialize-on-completion\n   387\t  \"Route one completion a materialization record claims, returning\n   388\t   [published records routes]. A :put-phase completion carrying :present\n   389\t   publishes nothing and moves the record to :verify-unissued -- the put\n   390\t   id's route dies with the completion, because no future completion can\n   391\t   bear an id already answered -- while every other transition removes\n   392\t   the record (the exactly-once guard) and publishes its one entry.\"\n   393\t  [completion record published records routes]\n   394\t  (let [{:keys [id lost answer]} completion\n   395\t        finish\n   396\t        (fn [tail]\n   397\t          [(conj published (merge (materialization-entry record) tail))\n   398\t           (dissoc records (get record :put-id))\n   399\t           (dissoc routes id)])]\n   400\t    (cond\n   401\t      lost (finish {:lost lost})\n   402\t\n   403\t      (contains? (:request completion) get-op)\n   404\t      (cond\n   405\t        (not (get-answer? answer)) (finish {:error malformed-response})\n   406\t        (not (get answer :jing/found?)) (finish {:error present-but-absent})\n   407\t        :else\n   408\t        (let [value (accepted-value (get record :address)\n   409\t                                    (get answer :jing/bytes))]\n   410\t          (if (identical? refused value)\n   411\t            (finish {:error integrity-failure})\n   412\t            (finish {:result :present}))))\n   413\t\n   414\t      :else\n   415\t      (let [verdict (and (put-answer? answer)\n   416\t                         (get answer :jing/result))]\n   417\t        (cond\n   418\t          (= :inserted verdict) (finish {:result :inserted})\n   419\t          (= :present verdict)\n   420\t          [published\n   421\t           (assoc records (get record :put-id)\n   422\t                  (assoc record :phase :verify-unissued))\n   423\t           (dissoc routes id)]\n   424\t          :else (finish {:error malformed-response}))))))\n   425\t\n   426\t\n   427\t(defn- route-completions\n   428\t  \"Order 5's routing: fold the drained completions against the live\n   429\t   records, then return the published entries and the successor records\n   430\t   and routes.\"\n   431\t  [completions records routes]\n   432\t  (let [[published records routes]\n   433\t        (reduce (fn [[published records routes] completion]\n   434\t                  (if-some [put-id (get routes (:id completion))]\n   435\t                    (if-some [record (get records put-id)]\n   436\t                      (materialize-on-completion\n   437\t                        completion record published records routes)\n   438\t                      [(conj published (decode-plain-completion completion))\n   439\t                       records\n   440\t                       routes])\n   441\t                    [(conj published (decode-plain-completion completion))\n   442\t                     records\n   443\t                     routes]))\n   444\t                [[] records routes]\n   445\t                completions)]\n   446\t    {:published published :records records :routes routes}))\n   447\t\n   448\t\n   449\t;; =============================================================================\n   450\t;; Orders 2 to 4 -- the polls and the verify reads\n   451\t;; =============================================================================\n   452\t\n   453\t\n   454\t(defn- lose-outstanding\n   455\t  \"Complete every outstanding request with `reason` -- each loss routes\n   456\t   through its claim at order 5, so a materialization's record finishes\n   457\t   exactly once. A terminal reason also ends the binding.\"\n   458\t  [state reason terminal?]\n   459\t  (let [state (reduce (fn [s [id request]]\n   460\t                        (update s :completed\n   461\t                                conj {:id id, :request request,\n   462\t                                      :lost reason}))\n   463\t                      state\n   464\t                      (:outstanding state))]\n   465\t    (cond-> (assoc state :outstanding {})\n   466\t      terminal? (assoc :terminal reason))))\n   467\t\n   468\t\n   469\t(defn- mint-cursor\n   470\t  \"Resolve an anchor-keyword cursor through the answers reader: the\n   471\t   Linda mint (:dao.stream/newest) on a reflection is answered across\n   472\t   the channel, so a retryable answer leaves the anchor in place for\n   473\t   the next step. Returns [cursor settled?].\"\n   474\t  [answers anchor]\n   475\t  (let [r (stream/cursor answers anchor)]\n   476\t    (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   477\t      [(:dao.stream/cursor r) true]\n   478\t      [anchor false])))\n   479\t\n   480\t\n   481\t(defn- poll\n   482\t  \"Order 2: read at most `budget` answers, correlating each by its\n   483\t   :jing/request id. A blocked read stops the step; a gap loses the\n   484\t   outstanding requests without ending the binding; a reader that ends,\n   485\t   errs, or answers an unrecognized outcome ends it. Non-answer values\n   486\t   and answers nobody claims are filed as diagnostics, taken exactly\n   487\t   once.\"\n   488\t  [state budget]\n   489\t  (loop [state state\n   490\t         left budget]\n   491\t    (cond\n   492\t      (:terminal state) state\n   493\t\n   494\t      (contains? stream/standard-anchors (:cursor state))\n   495\t      (let [[cursor settled?] (mint-cursor (:answers state)\n   496\t                                           (:cursor state))]\n   497\t        (if settled? (recur (assoc state :cursor cursor) left) state))\n   498\t\n   499\t      (zero? left) state\n   500\t\n   501\t      :else\n   502\t      (let [r (stream/next (:answers state) (:cursor state))\n   503\t            outcome (:dao.stream/outcome r)]\n   504\t        (cond\n   505\t          (= :dao.stream/ok outcome)\n   506\t          (let [v (:dao.stream/value r)\n   507\t                state (assoc state :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))]\n   508\t            (if-not (answer? v)\n   509\t              (recur (update state :diagnostics\n   510\t                             conj {:code :dao.jing.content/malformed-answer\n   511\t                                   :value v})\n   512\t                     (dec left))\n   513\t              (let [id (get v :jing/request)]\n   514\t                (if-some [request (get (:outstanding state) id)]\n   515\t                  (recur (-> state\n   516\t                             (update :outstanding dissoc id)\n   517\t                             (update :completed\n   518\t                                     conj {:id id, :request request,\n   519\t                                           :answer v}))\n   520\t                         (dec left))\n   521\t                  (recur (update state :diagnostics\n   522\t                                 conj {:code\n   523\t                                       :dao.jing.content/unsolicited-answer\n   524\t                                       :value v})\n   525\t                         (dec left))))))\n   526\t\n   527\t          (= :dao.stream/blocked outcome) state\n   528\t\n   529\t          (= :dao.stream/gap outcome)\n   530\t          (recur (lose-outstanding\n   531\t                   (assoc state :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   532\t                   :dao.stream/gap false)\n   533\t                 left)\n   534\t\n   535\t          :else\n   536\t          (recur (lose-outstanding state\n   537\t                                   (if (keyword? outcome)\n   538\t                                     outcome\n   539\t                                     :dao.stream/transport-error)\n   540\t                                   true)\n   541\t                 left))))))\n   542\t\n   543\t\n   544\t(defn- issue-pending-verifies\n   545\t  \"Order 4: issue the correlated verify reads of every :verify-unissued\n   546\t   record, in the order their puts were issued, until the writer\n   547\t   answers full (an unsent\n   548\t   request is all this client retains, so nothing else can be submitted\n   549\t   behind it) or the state is terminal -- a terminal state completes\n   550\t   each remaining record's loss here, because no wire completion will\n   551\t   ever bear its claim.\"\n   552\t  [state]\n   553\t  (loop [state state\n   554\t         pending (seq (sort-by (fn [[_id record]] (:seq record))\n   555\t                               (filter (fn [[_id record]]\n   556\t                                         (= :verify-unissued\n   557\t                                            (:phase record)))\n   558\t                                       (:materializations state))))]\n   559\t    (if (nil? pending)\n   560\t      state\n   561\t      (let [[put-id record] (first pending)]\n   562\t        (cond\n   563\t          (:terminal state)\n   564\t          (recur (-> state\n   565\t                     (update :completed\n   566\t                             conj (merge (materialization-entry record)\n   567\t                                         {:lost (:terminal state)}))\n   568\t                     (update :materializations dissoc put-id))\n   569\t                 (next pending))\n   570\t\n   571\t          (:unsent state) state\n   572\t\n   573\t          :else\n   574\t          (let [id (mint-id state)\n   575\t                request {get-op (:address record)}\n   576\t                result (stream/append! (:requests state)\n   577\t                                       (assoc request :jing/request id))\n   578\t                outcome (:dao.stream/outcome result)\n   579\t                state (assoc-in state\n   580\t                                [:materializations put-id :get-id] id)]\n   581\t            (cond\n   582\t              (= :dao.stream/ok outcome)\n   583\t              (recur (-> state\n   584\t                         (assoc-in [:outstanding id] request)\n   585\t                         (assoc-in [:routes id] put-id)\n   586\t                         (update :materializations assoc-in\n   587\t                                 [put-id :phase] :verify-issued))\n   588\t                     (next pending))\n   589\t\n   590\t              (= :dao.stream/full outcome)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
