{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc | sed -n '1170,1310p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc | sed -n '1550,1820p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1170\t(defn- answer-text\n  1171\t  \"Step 2's read: the Base64 reply text one content-pair answer carries,\n  1172\t   or `missing` when it carries none -- not found, or a value that is\n  1173\t   not the answer's text shape. A failing read has no payload for this\n  1174\t   link, so it fails closed as `:absent`, never as execution. Nothing is\n  1175\t   decoded here, so that step 2's byte cap runs before the text is.\"\n  1176\t  [answer]\n  1177\t  (if (and (map? answer)\n  1178\t           (true? (get answer :jing/found?))\n  1179\t           (string? (get answer :jing/bytes)))\n  1180\t    (get answer :jing/bytes)\n  1181\t    missing))\n  1182\t\n  1183\t\n  1184\t(defn- least-decoded-length\n  1185\t  \"The fewest bytes Base64 text of `text`'s length can decode to: strict\n  1186\t   padded Base64 of n characters is 3n/4 bytes less at most two of\n  1187\t   padding. Text over the budget by this measure is over it however it\n  1188\t   decodes, so it is refused without being decoded; text within it is\n  1189\t   decoded and meets the exact decoded-length cap.\"\n  1190\t  [text]\n  1191\t  (- (* 3 (quot (count text) 4)) 2))\n  1192\t\n  1193\t\n  1194\t(defn- ingress!\n  1195\t  \"The one ingress check, dao.jing/accept-bytes!, guarded: the canonical\n  1196\t   bytes the answer text carries for `address`, or a refusal mapping the\n  1197\t   check's reason onto step 2's closed refusal set. Text that is not\n  1198\t   strict Base64 has no payload (:absent); bytes that do not hash to the\n  1199\t   address, or that do not decode as exactly one canonical payload, are\n  1200\t   not the content the address names (:address-mismatch).\"\n  1201\t  [address text]\n  1202\t  (try\n  1203\t    {:bytes (jing/accept-bytes! address text)}\n  1204\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n  1205\t      (case (get (ex-data e) :reason)\n  1206\t        :base64 {:refusal (refused :absent {:address address})}\n  1207\t        {:refusal (refused :address-mismatch\n  1208\t                           (cond-> {:address address}\n  1209\t                             (= :non-canonical (get (ex-data e) :reason))\n  1210\t                             (assoc :value nil)))}))))\n  1211\t\n  1212\t\n  1213\t(defn- decoded\n  1214\t  \"The value of canonical bytes bs, or nil when they do not decode.\"\n  1215\t  [bs]\n  1216\t  (try (cbor/decode bs)\n  1217\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n  1218\t         nil)))\n  1219\t\n  1220\t\n  1221\t(defn- byte-count\n  1222\t  \"The length of host bytes bs, for the `:max-bytes` bound.\"\n  1223\t  [bs]\n  1224\t  #?(:clj (alength ^bytes bs)\n  1225\t     :cljs (.-length bs)\n  1226\t     :cljd (.-length ^typed/Uint8List bs)))\n  1227\t\n  1228\t\n  1229\t(defn- identity-of\n  1230\t  \"The identity `value` mints under the format, or nil when it cannot be\n  1231\t   minted at all (a malformed payload mints no identity). Used by\n  1232\t   `publish!` and for refusal evidence, never by verification: step 3 is\n  1233\t   `:identity-matches-fn`, directed by the identity the request carries\n  1234\t   (I5).\"\n  1235\t  [format value]\n  1236\t  (try ((:identity-fn format) value)\n  1237\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n  1238\t         nil)))\n  1239\t\n  1240\t\n  1241\t(defn- matches-identity?\n  1242\t  \"Step 3's check, directed by the identity the request carries. False\n  1243\t   when the payload cannot be matched at all (a malformed payload\n  1244\t   matches no identity).\"\n  1245\t  [format identity value]\n  1246\t  (try ((:identity-matches-fn format) identity value)\n  1247\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ false)))\n  1248\t\n  1249\t\n  1250\t(defn- row-defect\n  1251\t  \"Step 2's per-part check, or nil when the part is locally well formed.\n  1252\t   A `:row-defect-fn` that throws refuses like a validator.\"\n  1253\t  [format value]\n  1254\t  (try ((:row-defect-fn format) value)\n  1255\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n  1256\t         {:rule :validator-refused})))\n  1257\t\n  1258\t\n  1259\t(defn- validation-defect\n  1260\t  [format value]\n  1261\t  (try ((:validate-fn format) value)\n  1262\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n  1263\t         {:rule :validator-refused})))\n  1264\t\n  1265\t\n  1266\t(defn- checked-part\n  1267\t  \"One worklist visit over the Base64 reply `text` the content pair\n  1268\t   answered for `address`: bound the text against the byte `budget`\n  1269\t   remaining before it is decoded at all, admit it through the one\n  1270\t   ingress check, check the admitted size against the budget, then\n  1271\t   validate the part row-locally -- in that order, so an oversized\n  1272\t   reply is refused before its text is decoded, text that is not strict\n  1273\t   Base64 or bytes that fail the ingress check are refused before the\n  1274\t   row is seen, and a malformed row is refused before anything it\n  1275\t   references is decoded or enqueued. The order is total: no reply\n  1276\t   (`:absent`), then the text bound (`:parts-limit`), then the ingress\n  1277\t   refusal (`:absent` or `:address-mismatch`), then the decoded bound\n  1278\t   (`:parts-limit`). Returns `{:value v :bytes n}` or a refusal.\"\n  1279\t  [format identity address text budget]\n  1280\t  (cond\n  1281\t    (identical? missing text)\n  1282\t    (refused :absent {:address address})\n  1283\t\n  1284\t    (and budget (> (least-decoded-length text) budget))\n  1285\t    (refused :parts-limit {:bound :max-bytes, :address address})\n  1286\t\n  1287\t    :else\n  1288\t    (let [ingress (ingress! address text)]\n  1289\t      (if-some [refusal (:refusal ingress)]\n  1290\t        refusal\n  1291\t        (let [bs (:bytes ingress)]\n  1292\t          (if (and budget (> (byte-count bs) budget))\n  1293\t            (refused :parts-limit {:bound :max-bytes, :address address})\n  1294\t            (let [value (decoded bs)]\n  1295\t              (if (nil? value)\n  1296\t                (refused :address-mismatch {:address address, :value nil})\n  1297\t                (if-let [defect (row-defect format value)]\n  1298\t                  (refused :descriptor-defect\n  1299\t                           {:identity identity, :address address,\n  1300\t                            :defect defect})\n  1301\t                  {:value value, :bytes (byte-count bs)})))))))))\n  1302\t\n  1303\t\n  1304\t(def default-bounds\n  1305\t  \"The safe finite composition bounds a fetch falls back to where the\n  1306\t   caller supplies none (section 4.2 step 2): generous for every honest\n  1307\t   image the compositions hold, finite for a hostile one, so no fetch\n  1308\t   path walks an unbounded worklist.\"\n  1309\t  {:max-parts 4096, :max-depth 256, :max-bytes 16777216})\n  1310\t\n  1550\t  \"The completion of link `id` for `outcome` (section 6.3): the verified\n  1551\t   image under `:image` with its obligations beside it, or the refusal\n  1552\t   or loss tagged with the id.\"\n  1553\t  [id outcome]\n  1554\t  (if (ok? outcome)\n  1555\t    {:yin.link/id id,\n  1556\t     :status :ok,\n  1557\t     :image (dissoc outcome :status :obligations),\n  1558\t     :obligations (:obligations outcome)}\n  1559\t    (assoc outcome :yin.link/id id)))\n  1560\t\n  1561\t\n  1562\t(defn- finish\n  1563\t  \"Retire link `id`'s bookkeeping and append its one completion.\"\n  1564\t  [state id outcome]\n  1565\t  (-> state\n  1566\t      (update :links dissoc id)\n  1567\t      (update :order (fn [order] (filterv (fn [x] (not= id x)) order)))\n  1568\t      (update :outbox conj (completion id outcome))))\n  1569\t\n  1570\t\n  1571\t(defn request-link\n  1572\t  \"Admit one link request (section 6.3) and return `[state link-id]`.\n  1573\t   `request` is plain data: `:yin.link/id`, `:yin.link/format`,\n  1574\t   `:yin.link/contract`, and exactly one of `:yin.link/name` or\n  1575\t   `:yin.link/identity`. Admission (step 0) and the index lookup (step\n  1576\t   1) touch no stream, so a request they refuse completes at the next\n  1577\t   `step` under its id -- or under `:yin.link/id nil` when the id is not\n  1578\t   a well-formed `[origin counter]` pair or already names a link whose\n  1579\t   completion is owed. Nothing is sent here: `step` issues every content\n  1580\t   request.\"\n  1581\t  [state request]\n  1582\t  (let [raw-id (when (map? request) (:yin.link/id request))\n  1583\t        duplicate? (and (link-id? raw-id) (in-flight? state raw-id))\n  1584\t        id (when (and (link-id? raw-id) (not duplicate?)) raw-id)\n  1585\t        defect (cond\n  1586\t                 (not (map? request))\n  1587\t                 (refused :invalid-request {:defect :not-a-map})\n  1588\t\n  1589\t                 duplicate?\n  1590\t                 (refused :invalid-request {:defect :duplicate-id})\n  1591\t\n  1592\t                 (nil? id)\n  1593\t                 (refused :invalid-request {:defect :id})\n  1594\t\n  1595\t                 :else (request-defect state request))\n  1596\t        address (when-not defect (root-address state request))]\n  1597\t    (cond\n  1598\t      defect [(update state :outbox conj (completion id defect)) id]\n  1599\t      (refused? address) [(update state :outbox conj (completion id address))\n  1600\t                          id]\n  1601\t      :else\n  1602\t      [(-> state\n  1603\t           (assoc-in [:links id]\n  1604\t                     {:format (:yin.link/format request),\n  1605\t                      :identity (:yin.link/identity request),\n  1606\t                      :address address,\n  1607\t                      :queue [[address 0]],\n  1608\t                      :at 0,\n  1609\t                      :parts {},\n  1610\t                      :bytes 0,\n  1611\t                      :enqueued #{address},\n  1612\t                      :awaiting nil})\n  1613\t           (update :order conj id))\n  1614\t       id])))\n  1615\t\n  1616\t\n  1617\t(defn- receive-part\n  1618\t  \"Route the reply `text` answered for link `id`'s current worklist entry\n  1619\t   through step 2's checks; enqueue the part's children under the parts\n  1620\t   budget; and, when the worklist is empty, run steps 3 to 5a at once\n  1621\t   (section 6.3: they never touch a stream).\"\n  1622\t  [state id text]\n  1623\t  (let [link (get-in state [:links id])\n  1624\t        {:keys [queue at parts bytes enqueued]} link\n  1625\t        record (get (:formats state) (:format link))\n  1626\t        {:keys [max-parts max-bytes]} (:bounds state)\n  1627\t        [address depth] (nth queue at)\n  1628\t        res (checked-part record (:identity link) address text\n  1629\t                          (when max-bytes (- max-bytes bytes)))]\n  1630\t    (if (refused? res)\n  1631\t      (finish state id res)\n  1632\t      (let [value (:value res)\n  1633\t            enqueued' (enqueue-children ((:parts-fn record) value)\n  1634\t                                        enqueued depth max-parts)]\n  1635\t        (if (refused? enqueued')\n  1636\t          (finish state id enqueued')\n  1637\t          (let [link' (assoc link\n  1638\t                             :queue (into queue (:queue enqueued'))\n  1639\t                             :at (inc at)\n  1640\t                             :parts (assoc parts address value)\n  1641\t                             :bytes (+ bytes (:bytes res))\n  1642\t                             :enqueued (into enqueued (:fresh enqueued'))\n  1643\t                             :awaiting nil)]\n  1644\t            (if (= (:at link') (count (:queue link')))\n  1645\t              (finish state id (verify record (:identity link)\n  1646\t                                       (:address link) (:parts link')))\n  1647\t              (assoc-in state [:links id] link'))))))))\n  1648\t\n  1649\t\n  1650\t(defn- mint-request-id\n  1651\t  \"A self-minted random request id (the content vocabulary's r), unique\n  1652\t   against the ids this client owes, so an answer correlates to the link\n  1653\t   that asked and callers sharing one answers stream do not collide.\"\n  1654\t  [state]\n  1655\t  (loop []\n  1656\t    (let [id (str (random-uuid))]\n  1657\t      (if (or (contains? (:routes state) id)\n  1658\t              (= id (get-in state [:content :unsent :id])))\n  1659\t        (recur)\n  1660\t        id))))\n  1661\t\n  1662\t\n  1663\t(defn- route-answer\n  1664\t  \"Route one content-pair answer to the link awaiting its id: the entry\n  1665\t   carries the raw answer, or a loss with its reason, and a loss routes\n  1666\t   exactly as a reply that carried no payload does (checked-part's\n  1667\t   `missing`). An id no link claims -- the late answer of an abandoned\n  1668\t   link -- is dropped.\"\n  1669\t  [state entry]\n  1670\t  (let [rid (:id entry)\n  1671\t        id (get (:routes state) rid)]\n  1672\t    (if (and (some? id) (contains? (:links state) id))\n  1673\t      (receive-part (update state :routes dissoc rid)\n  1674\t                    id (answer-text (:answer entry)))\n  1675\t      (update state :routes dissoc rid))))\n  1676\t\n  1677\t\n  1678\t(defn- lose-claims\n  1679\t  \"Mark every claim the content client holds lost with `reason`: each\n  1680\t   id's loss routes on the ordinary path, its route dying there as any\n  1681\t   answer's does. A terminal reason also ends the client, and the one\n  1682\t   retained unsent request dies with it: no later step can deliver it.\"\n  1683\t  [state reason terminal?]\n  1684\t  (let [losses (mapv (fn [rid] {:id rid, :lost reason})\n  1685\t                     (keys (:routes state)))\n  1686\t        state (cond-> state\n  1687\t                (and terminal? (get-in state [:content :unsent]))\n  1688\t                (assoc-in [:content :unsent] nil)\n  1689\t\n  1690\t                terminal?\n  1691\t                (assoc-in [:content :terminal] reason))]\n  1692\t    [state losses]))\n  1693\t\n  1694\t\n  1695\t(defn- anchor-cursor\n  1696\t  \"Resolve an anchor-keyword cursor through the answers reader: the\n  1697\t   Linda mint (:dao.stream/newest) on a reflection is answered across\n  1698\t   the channel, so an answer that is not yet available leaves the anchor\n  1699\t   in place for the next step. Returns [cursor settled?].\"\n  1700\t  [answers anchor]\n  1701\t  (let [r (stream/cursor answers anchor)]\n  1702\t    (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n  1703\t      [(:dao.stream/cursor r) true]\n  1704\t      [anchor false])))\n  1705\t\n  1706\t\n  1707\t(defn- poll-answers\n  1708\t  \"Order 2: read at most `budget` answers, correlating each by its\n  1709\t   :jing/request id against the claims in :routes. Returns\n  1710\t   {:state s :routed [...] :diagnostics [...]}: each answer a claim\n  1711\t   holds is routed under its id; an answer nobody claims, or a value\n  1712\t   that is not an answer, is a diagnostic and never reaches a link. A\n  1713\t   blocked read stops the poll; a gap loses every claim without ending\n  1714\t   the client; a reader that ends or errs ends it, the losses routed\n  1715\t   with the outcome as their reason.\"\n  1716\t  [state budget]\n  1717\t  (loop [state state, left budget, routed [], diagnostics []]\n  1718\t    (cond\n  1719\t      (:terminal (:content state))\n  1720\t      {:state state, :routed routed, :diagnostics diagnostics}\n  1721\t\n  1722\t      (contains? stream/standard-anchors (:cursor (:content state)))\n  1723\t      (let [[cursor settled?]\n  1724\t            (anchor-cursor (:answers (:content state))\n  1725\t                           (:cursor (:content state)))]\n  1726\t        (if settled?\n  1727\t          (recur (assoc-in state [:content :cursor] cursor)\n  1728\t                 left routed diagnostics)\n  1729\t          {:state state, :routed routed, :diagnostics diagnostics}))\n  1730\t\n  1731\t      (zero? left)\n  1732\t      {:state state, :routed routed, :diagnostics diagnostics}\n  1733\t\n  1734\t      :else\n  1735\t      (let [r (stream/next (:answers (:content state))\n  1736\t                           (:cursor (:content state)))\n  1737\t            outcome (:dao.stream/outcome r)]\n  1738\t        (cond\n  1739\t          (= :dao.stream/ok outcome)\n  1740\t          (let [v (:dao.stream/value r)\n  1741\t                state (assoc-in state [:content :cursor]\n  1742\t                                (:dao.stream/cursor r))]\n  1743\t            (if (and (map? v) (contains? v :jing/request))\n  1744\t              (let [rid (get v :jing/request)]\n  1745\t                (if (contains? (:routes state) rid)\n  1746\t                  (recur state (dec left)\n  1747\t                         (conj routed {:id rid, :answer v}) diagnostics)\n  1748\t                  (recur state (dec left) routed\n  1749\t                         (conj diagnostics\n  1750\t                               {:yin.link/code :yin.link/unsolicited-answer\n  1751\t                                :yin.link/value v}))))\n  1752\t              (recur state (dec left) routed\n  1753\t                     (conj diagnostics\n  1754\t                           {:yin.link/code :yin.link/malformed-answer\n  1755\t                            :yin.link/value v}))))\n  1756\t\n  1757\t          (= :dao.stream/blocked outcome)\n  1758\t          {:state state, :routed routed, :diagnostics diagnostics}\n  1759\t\n  1760\t          (= :dao.stream/gap outcome)\n  1761\t          (let [[state losses]\n  1762\t                (lose-claims\n  1763\t                  (assoc-in state [:content :cursor] (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n  1764\t                  :dao.stream/gap false)]\n  1765\t            (recur state left (into routed losses) diagnostics))\n  1766\t\n  1767\t          :else\n  1768\t          (let [reason (if (keyword? outcome)\n  1769\t                         outcome\n  1770\t                         :dao.stream/transport-error)\n  1771\t                [state losses] (lose-claims state reason true)]\n  1772\t            (recur state left (into routed losses) diagnostics)))))))\n  1773\t\n  1774\t\n  1775\t(defn- issue-request\n  1776\t  \"Issue link `id`'s next content request, in worklist order, unless one\n  1777\t   is already awaited. The depth bound is checked before the read; a\n  1778\t   terminal client has no payload for the link (`:absent`, failing\n  1779\t   closed); a writer still owing an unsent request issues nothing this\n  1780\t   step -- the client retains one request, retried by the next step. A\n  1781\t   writer that refuses the append outright files the loss for the next\n  1782\t   step's routing, through the claim the issue already holds.\"\n  1783\t  [state id]\n  1784\t  (let [link (get-in state [:links id])\n  1785\t        content (:content state)]\n  1786\t    (if (or (nil? link) (some? (:awaiting link)))\n  1787\t      state\n  1788\t      (let [[address depth] (nth (:queue link) (:at link))\n  1789\t            max-depth (:max-depth (:bounds state))]\n  1790\t        (cond\n  1791\t          (and max-depth (> depth max-depth))\n  1792\t          (finish state id\n  1793\t                  (refused :parts-limit {:bound :max-depth, :address address}))\n  1794\t\n  1795\t          (:terminal content)\n  1796\t          (finish state id (refused :absent {:address address}))\n  1797\t\n  1798\t          (:unsent content)\n  1799\t          state\n  1800\t\n  1801\t          :else\n  1802\t          (let [rid (mint-request-id state)\n  1803\t                value {:jing/request rid, :jing/get address}\n  1804\t                outcome (:dao.stream/outcome\n  1805\t                          (stream/append! (:requests content) value))]\n  1806\t            (case outcome\n  1807\t              (:dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/full)\n  1808\t              (-> state\n  1809\t                  (cond-> (= :dao.stream/full outcome)\n  1810\t                    (assoc-in [:content :unsent]\n  1811\t                              {:id rid, :value value}))\n  1812\t                  (assoc-in [:links id :awaiting] rid)\n  1813\t                  (assoc-in [:routes rid] id))\n  1814\t\n  1815\t              ;; closed, invalid-value, refused, transport-error: the\n  1816\t              ;; append never happened, and the loss is filed for the\n  1817\t              ;; next step's routing under the claim just taken\n  1818\t              (-> state\n  1819\t                  (assoc-in [:links id :awaiting] rid)\n  1820\t                  (assoc-in [:routes rid] id)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/jing/content/step.cljc | sed -n '100,225p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/jing/content/step.cljc | sed -n '225,390p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/jing/content/step.cljc | sed -n '390,565p'\"","aggregated_output":"   100\t\n   101\t(def ^:private integrity-failure\n   102\t  \"The error map a failed ingress check publishes, by code.\"\n   103\t  {:code integrity-failure-code\n   104\t   :message \"the remote content does not hash to its content address\"})\n   105\t\n   106\t\n   107\t(def ^:private malformed-response\n   108\t  \"The error map for an answer outside its request's vocabulary.\"\n   109\t  {:code malformed-response-code\n   110\t   :message \"the answer does not conform to the request's vocabulary\"})\n   111\t\n   112\t\n   113\t(def ^:private present-but-absent\n   114\t  {:code present-but-absent-code\n   115\t   :message \"the remote reported :present but the content address is absent\"})\n   116\t\n   117\t\n   118\t(defn- mint-id\n   119\t  \"A self-minted random request id, unique against this client's live\n   120\t   ids so callers sharing one answers stream do not collide.\"\n   121\t  [state]\n   122\t  (loop []\n   123\t    (let [id (str (random-uuid))]\n   124\t      (if (or (contains? (:outstanding state) id)\n   125\t              (= id (get-in state [:unsent :id])))\n   126\t        (recur)\n   127\t        id))))\n   128\t\n   129\t\n   130\t(defn- answer?\n   131\t  \"True for any well-formed answer value: the request id key, whatever\n   132\t   body follows it.\"\n   133\t  [v]\n   134\t  (and (map? v) (contains? v :jing/request)))\n   135\t\n   136\t\n   137\t;; =============================================================================\n   138\t;; State\n   139\t;; =============================================================================\n   140\t\n   141\t\n   142\t(defn client-state\n   143\t  \"The stepped client's state over one content pair: `requests` the\n   144\t   writer the client appends its requests to, `answers` the reader it\n   145\t   polls, `cursor` either a cursor `answers` handed out or an anchor\n   146\t   keyword (:dao.stream/newest, the Linda mint, resolved on the first\n   147\t   poll -- a reflection's mint is answered across the channel, so the\n   148\t   first steps may retry it). The caller owns the result and every step\n   149\t   of it.\"\n   150\t  [requests answers cursor]\n   151\t  {:requests requests\n   152\t   :answers answers\n   153\t   :cursor cursor\n   154\t   :unsent nil\n   155\t   :outstanding {}\n   156\t   :completed []\n   157\t   :diagnostics []\n   158\t   :terminal nil\n   159\t   :next-seq 0\n   160\t   :materializations {}\n   161\t   :routes {}})\n   162\t\n   163\t\n   164\t(defn- segment-address!\n   165\t  \"Throw unless `address` is a segment address: arbitrary keys and\n   166\t   mutable roots are refused before the wire.\"\n   167\t  [address]\n   168\t  (when-not (jing/segment-address? address)\n   169\t    (throw (ex-info \"a stepped content request names a non-segment address\"\n   170\t                    {:address address}))))\n   171\t\n   172\t\n   173\t(defn- register\n   174\t  \"Claim `id` for a materialization: the record (carrying its issue\n   175\t   order under :seq -- the ids are random, so the order the verify reads\n   176\t   issue in is the record's own) and its route.\"\n   177\t  [state id address]\n   178\t  (-> state\n   179\t      (assoc-in [:materializations id]\n   180\t                {:phase :put, :address address, :put-id id\n   181\t                 :seq (:next-seq state)})\n   182\t      (update :next-seq (fnil inc 0))\n   183\t      (assoc-in [:routes id] id)))\n   184\t\n   185\t\n   186\t(defn- submit\n   187\t  \"The shared body of the request entry points: answer :terminal on a\n   188\t   client whose answers reader has ended (a new pair is a new client),\n   189\t   refuse with :busy while an unsent request is owed (only step's order\n   190\t   1 clears it), append the request value, and register a\n   191\t   materialization record at any id the writer's answer carries. A\n   192\t   writer refusal completes at once -- the record routes that loss at\n   193\t   the next drain.\"\n   194\t  [state request materialize?]\n   195\t  (cond\n   196\t    (:terminal state)\n   197\t    {:outcome :terminal, :state state}\n   198\t\n   199\t    (:unsent state)\n   200\t    {:outcome :busy, :state state}\n   201\t\n   202\t    :else\n   203\t    (let [id (mint-id state)\n   204\t          value (assoc request :jing/request id)\n   205\t          result (stream/append! (:requests state) value)\n   206\t          outcome (:dao.stream/outcome result)\n   207\t          address (get request put-op)]\n   208\t      (cond\n   209\t        (= :dao.stream/ok outcome)\n   210\t        {:outcome :requested\n   211\t         :state (-> (assoc-in state [:outstanding id] request)\n   212\t                    (cond-> materialize? (register id address)))\n   213\t         :id id}\n   214\t\n   215\t        (= :dao.stream/full outcome)\n   216\t        {:outcome :pending-request\n   217\t         :state (-> (assoc state :unsent {:id id, :value value})\n   218\t                    (cond-> materialize? (register id address)))\n   219\t         :id id}\n   220\t\n   221\t        :else\n   222\t        ;; closed, invalid-value, transport-error: the append never\n   223\t        ;; happened; the loss completes on the ordinary path\n   224\t        {:outcome :request-undeliverable\n   225\t         :state (-> (update state :completed\n   225\t         :state (-> (update state :completed\n   226\t                            conj {:id id, :request request, :lost outcome})\n   227\t                    (cond-> materialize? (register id address)))\n   228\t         :id id\n   229\t         :reason outcome}))))\n   230\t\n   231\t\n   232\t;; =============================================================================\n   233\t;; The request entry points\n   234\t;; =============================================================================\n   235\t\n   236\t\n   237\t(defn request-get\n   238\t  \"Request one remote read of `address`. A non-segment address throws\n   239\t   before the wire. While an unsent request is owed the answer is\n   240\t   {:outcome :busy :state s} and nothing was submitted; otherwise the\n   241\t   outcome is returned with the minted id under :id, and the read's\n   242\t   completion arrives through step as {:id s :found? b :value v} (or an\n   243\t   :error, or a :lost tail).\"\n   244\t  [state address]\n   245\t  (segment-address! address)\n   246\t  (submit state {get-op address} false))\n   247\t\n   248\t\n   249\t(defn request-put\n   250\t  \"Request one remote put of `payload` at `address`. A non-segment\n   251\t   address throws before the wire; address-against-payload validation is\n   252\t   the server's at its own door, and a mismatch is the server's silence.\n   253\t   A plain put publishes :result :inserted or :result :present with no\n   254\t   verify read: the read-back is materialization's obligation.\"\n   255\t  [state address payload]\n   256\t  (segment-address! address)\n   257\t  (submit state {put-op address\n   258\t                 :jing/bytes (jing/bytes->base64\n   259\t                               (jing/canonical-bytes payload))}\n   260\t          false))\n   261\t\n   262\t\n   263\t(defn request-put-bytes\n   264\t  \"The bytes-level twin of request-put for a caller already holding the\n   265\t   canonical payload bytes -- the byte-store handle's own put. The bytes\n   266\t   must hash to `address`; the server's ingress check refuses them\n   267\t   otherwise, and a refused request is the server's silence.\"\n   268\t  [state address bs]\n   269\t  (segment-address! address)\n   270\t  (submit state {put-op address\n   271\t                 :jing/bytes (jing/bytes->base64 bs)}\n   272\t          false))\n   273\t\n   274\t\n   275\t(defn request-materialize\n   276\t  \"Request one remote materialization of `payload`: the address is\n   277\t   derived here, the put is submitted, and the returned :id is the put\n   278\t   id the one completion will carry. Supports an explicit algorithm via\n   279\t   opts: {:algorithm :sha256}.\"\n   280\t  ([state payload] (request-materialize state payload {}))\n   281\t  ([state payload opts]\n   282\t   (let [bs (jing/canonical-bytes payload)\n   283\t         algo (get opts :algorithm jing/default-hash-algorithm)\n   284\t         reg (get jing/registry algo)]\n   285\t     (when-not reg\n   286\t       (throw (ex-info (str \"unsupported hash algorithm: \" algo)\n   287\t                       {:algorithm algo})))\n   288\t     (let [address (keyword \"segment\"\n   289\t                            (str (:address-id reg)\n   290\t                                 \"-\" (jing/digest-bytes algo bs)))]\n   291\t       (submit state {put-op address\n   292\t                      :jing/bytes (jing/bytes->base64 bs)}\n   293\t               true)))))\n   294\t\n   295\t\n   296\t(def ^:private refused\n   297\t  \"The ingress-refusal sentinel for the strict receipt decode below: one\n   298\t   opaque host object held by this single var, so every reference to it\n   299\t   is the same instance on every host. A keyword literal cannot serve:\n   300\t   on cljs each literal site compiles to a fresh Keyword object, so an\n   301\t   `identical?` across two sites misses, and a refused decode escaped\n   302\t   into the value arm. The closed CBOR profile never decodes a host\n   303\t   object, so no decoded value can be this; the sentinel itself is what\n   304\t   distinguishes a refused reply from a stored nil, which decodes to the\n   305\t   value nil.\"\n   306\t  #?(:cljd (Object.)\n   307\t     :clj (Object.)\n   308\t     :cljs (js-obj)))\n   309\t\n   310\t\n   311\t(defn- accepted-value\n   312\t  \"The value a found get answer carries, admitted through the one\n   313\t   ingress check (dao.jing/accept-bytes!) and decoded, or `refused` when\n   314\t   the check refuses it.\"\n   315\t  [address b64]\n   316\t  (try\n   317\t    (cbor/decode (jing/accept-bytes! address b64))\n   318\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   319\t      refused)))\n   320\t\n   321\t\n   322\t;; =============================================================================\n   323\t;; Completion decode\n   324\t;; =============================================================================\n   325\t\n   326\t\n   327\t(defn- get-answer?\n   328\t  \"True only for the exact read answer {:jing/request r :jing/found? b\n   329\t   :jing/bytes b64}.\"\n   330\t  [v]\n   331\t  (and (map? v)\n   332\t       (= #{:jing/request :jing/found? :jing/bytes} (set (keys v)))\n   333\t       (let [f (get v :jing/found?)] (or (true? f) (false? f)))))\n   334\t\n   335\t\n   336\t(defn- put-answer?\n   337\t  \"True only for the exact write answer {:jing/request r\n   338\t   :jing/result v}.\"\n   339\t  [v]\n   340\t  (and (map? v) (= #{:jing/request :jing/result} (set (keys v)))))\n   341\t\n   342\t\n   343\t(defn- decode-plain-completion\n   344\t  \"Total decode of one completion no materialization claims: the answer\n   345\t   conforms to its request's vocabulary or the completion carries an\n   346\t   :error; a loss carries :lost.\"\n   347\t  [completion]\n   348\t  (let [{:keys [id request lost answer]} completion]\n   349\t    (cond\n   350\t      lost {:id id, :lost lost}\n   351\t\n   352\t      (contains? request get-op)\n   353\t      (cond\n   354\t        (not (get-answer? answer)) {:id id, :error malformed-response}\n   355\t        (not (get answer :jing/found?))\n   356\t        {:id id, :found? false, :value nil}\n   357\t        :else\n   358\t        (let [value (accepted-value (get request get-op)\n   359\t                                    (get answer :jing/bytes))]\n   360\t          (if (identical? refused value)\n   361\t            {:id id, :error integrity-failure}\n   362\t            {:id id, :found? true, :value value})))\n   363\t\n   364\t      :else\n   365\t      (if (and (put-answer? answer)\n   366\t               (#{:inserted :present} (get answer :jing/result)))\n   367\t        {:id id, :address (get request put-op),\n   368\t         :result (get answer :jing/result)}\n   369\t        {:id id, :error malformed-response}))))\n   370\t\n   371\t\n   372\t;; =============================================================================\n   373\t;; The materialization transition\n   374\t;; =============================================================================\n   375\t\n   376\t\n   377\t(defn- materialization-entry\n   378\t  \"The published tail of one materialization completion: the put id, the\n   379\t   marker, and the address -- never the payload.\"\n   380\t  [record]\n   381\t  {:id (get record :put-id)\n   382\t   :materialized? true\n   383\t   :address (get record :address)})\n   384\t\n   385\t\n   386\t(defn- materialize-on-completion\n   387\t  \"Route one completion a materialization record claims, returning\n   388\t   [published records routes]. A :put-phase completion carrying :present\n   389\t   publishes nothing and moves the record to :verify-unissued -- the put\n   390\t   id's route dies with the completion, because no future completion can\n   390\t   id's route dies with the completion, because no future completion can\n   391\t   bear an id already answered -- while every other transition removes\n   392\t   the record (the exactly-once guard) and publishes its one entry.\"\n   393\t  [completion record published records routes]\n   394\t  (let [{:keys [id lost answer]} completion\n   395\t        finish\n   396\t        (fn [tail]\n   397\t          [(conj published (merge (materialization-entry record) tail))\n   398\t           (dissoc records (get record :put-id))\n   399\t           (dissoc routes id)])]\n   400\t    (cond\n   401\t      lost (finish {:lost lost})\n   402\t\n   403\t      (contains? (:request completion) get-op)\n   404\t      (cond\n   405\t        (not (get-answer? answer)) (finish {:error malformed-response})\n   406\t        (not (get answer :jing/found?)) (finish {:error present-but-absent})\n   407\t        :else\n   408\t        (let [value (accepted-value (get record :address)\n   409\t                                    (get answer :jing/bytes))]\n   410\t          (if (identical? refused value)\n   411\t            (finish {:error integrity-failure})\n   412\t            (finish {:result :present}))))\n   413\t\n   414\t      :else\n   415\t      (let [verdict (and (put-answer? answer)\n   416\t                         (get answer :jing/result))]\n   417\t        (cond\n   418\t          (= :inserted verdict) (finish {:result :inserted})\n   419\t          (= :present verdict)\n   420\t          [published\n   421\t           (assoc records (get record :put-id)\n   422\t                  (assoc record :phase :verify-unissued))\n   423\t           (dissoc routes id)]\n   424\t          :else (finish {:error malformed-response}))))))\n   425\t\n   426\t\n   427\t(defn- route-completions\n   428\t  \"Order 5's routing: fold the drained completions against the live\n   429\t   records, then return the published entries and the successor records\n   430\t   and routes.\"\n   431\t  [completions records routes]\n   432\t  (let [[published records routes]\n   433\t        (reduce (fn [[published records routes] completion]\n   434\t                  (if-some [put-id (get routes (:id completion))]\n   435\t                    (if-some [record (get records put-id)]\n   436\t                      (materialize-on-completion\n   437\t                        completion record published records routes)\n   438\t                      [(conj published (decode-plain-completion completion))\n   439\t                       records\n   440\t                       routes])\n   441\t                    [(conj published (decode-plain-completion completion))\n   442\t                     records\n   443\t                     routes]))\n   444\t                [[] records routes]\n   445\t                completions)]\n   446\t    {:published published :records records :routes routes}))\n   447\t\n   448\t\n   449\t;; =============================================================================\n   450\t;; Orders 2 to 4 -- the polls and the verify reads\n   451\t;; =============================================================================\n   452\t\n   453\t\n   454\t(defn- lose-outstanding\n   455\t  \"Complete every outstanding request with `reason` -- each loss routes\n   456\t   through its claim at order 5, so a materialization's record finishes\n   457\t   exactly once. A terminal reason also ends the binding.\"\n   458\t  [state reason terminal?]\n   459\t  (let [state (reduce (fn [s [id request]]\n   460\t                        (update s :completed\n   461\t                                conj {:id id, :request request,\n   462\t                                      :lost reason}))\n   463\t                      state\n   464\t                      (:outstanding state))]\n   465\t    (cond-> (assoc state :outstanding {})\n   466\t      terminal? (assoc :terminal reason))))\n   467\t\n   468\t\n   469\t(defn- mint-cursor\n   470\t  \"Resolve an anchor-keyword cursor through the answers reader: the\n   471\t   Linda mint (:dao.stream/newest) on a reflection is answered across\n   472\t   the channel, so a retryable answer leaves the anchor in place for\n   473\t   the next step. Returns [cursor settled?].\"\n   474\t  [answers anchor]\n   475\t  (let [r (stream/cursor answers anchor)]\n   476\t    (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   477\t      [(:dao.stream/cursor r) true]\n   478\t      [anchor false])))\n   479\t\n   480\t\n   481\t(defn- poll\n   482\t  \"Order 2: read at most `budget` answers, correlating each by its\n   483\t   :jing/request id. A blocked read stops the step; a gap loses the\n   484\t   outstanding requests without ending the binding; a reader that ends,\n   485\t   errs, or answers an unrecognized outcome ends it. Non-answer values\n   486\t   and answers nobody claims are filed as diagnostics, taken exactly\n   487\t   once.\"\n   488\t  [state budget]\n   489\t  (loop [state state\n   490\t         left budget]\n   491\t    (cond\n   492\t      (:terminal state) state\n   493\t\n   494\t      (contains? stream/standard-anchors (:cursor state))\n   495\t      (let [[cursor settled?] (mint-cursor (:answers state)\n   496\t                                           (:cursor state))]\n   497\t        (if settled? (recur (assoc state :cursor cursor) left) state))\n   498\t\n   499\t      (zero? left) state\n   500\t\n   501\t      :else\n   502\t      (let [r (stream/next (:answers state) (:cursor state))\n   503\t            outcome (:dao.stream/outcome r)]\n   504\t        (cond\n   505\t          (= :dao.stream/ok outcome)\n   506\t          (let [v (:dao.stream/value r)\n   507\t                state (assoc state :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))]\n   508\t            (if-not (answer? v)\n   509\t              (recur (update state :diagnostics\n   510\t                             conj {:code :dao.jing.content/malformed-answer\n   511\t                                   :value v})\n   512\t                     (dec left))\n   513\t              (let [id (get v :jing/request)]\n   514\t                (if-some [request (get (:outstanding state) id)]\n   515\t                  (recur (-> state\n   516\t                             (update :outstanding dissoc id)\n   517\t                             (update :completed\n   518\t                                     conj {:id id, :request request,\n   519\t                                           :answer v}))\n   520\t                         (dec left))\n   521\t                  (recur (update state :diagnostics\n   522\t                                 conj {:code\n   523\t                                       :dao.jing.content/unsolicited-answer\n   524\t                                       :value v})\n   525\t                         (dec left))))))\n   526\t\n   527\t          (= :dao.stream/blocked outcome) state\n   528\t\n   529\t          (= :dao.stream/gap outcome)\n   530\t          (recur (lose-outstanding\n   531\t                   (assoc state :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   532\t                   :dao.stream/gap false)\n   533\t                 left)\n   534\t\n   535\t          :else\n   536\t          (recur (lose-outstanding state\n   537\t                                   (if (keyword? outcome)\n   538\t                                     outcome\n   539\t                                     :dao.stream/transport-error)\n   540\t                                   true)\n   541\t                 left))))))\n   542\t\n   543\t\n   544\t(defn- issue-pending-verifies\n   545\t  \"Order 4: issue the correlated verify reads of every :verify-unissued\n   546\t   record, in the order their puts were issued, until the writer\n   547\t   answers full (an unsent\n   548\t   request is all this client retains, so nothing else can be submitted\n   549\t   behind it) or the state is terminal -- a terminal state completes\n   550\t   each remaining record's loss here, because no wire completion will\n   551\t   ever bear its claim.\"\n   552\t  [state]\n   553\t  (loop [state state\n   554\t         pending (seq (sort-by (fn [[_id record]] (:seq record))\n   555\t                               (filter (fn [[_id record]]\n   556\t                                         (= :verify-unissued\n   557\t                                            (:phase record)))\n   558\t                                       (:materializations state))))]\n   559\t    (if (nil? pending)\n   560\t      state\n   561\t      (let [[put-id record] (first pending)]\n   562\t        (cond\n   563\t          (:terminal state)\n   564\t          (recur (-> state\n   565\t                     (update :completed\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
